    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Comfort",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a neural network for a school to predict whether its classrooms are comfortable or uncomfortable for students, based on the temperature of the room and the humidity.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Open the `classroom.csv` file and read the data into a variable called `rooms` that stores a list of rows.\r\n2. Fill in the `TODO`s in the definitions of `inputs` and `outputs` with names of columns from `classroom.csv`. For the first input, use the temperature of the room; for the second input, use the humidity of the room.\r\n3. Fit the model to the training input and output data.\r\n4. Score the model on the test input and output data. Print out the accuracy score.\r\n5. Run the program. Look at the accuracy score, then look at the visualization of the data and what the model learned. How well did the model learn the pattern in the data? You’ll answer a question about this in the next level.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nUse `open` to open a file and `csv.DictReader` to read that file into dictionaries.\r\n\r\nUse the `fit` method to train a model and the `score` method to score it. Both methods accept two arguments: a list of inputs and a list of outputs.\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Evaluate a neural network for a school to predict whether its classrooms are comfortable or uncomfortable for students.",
